course: dictionary
lesson: 13547
title: Imprisoned: trapped and kept in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imprisoned is the past tense of imprison, so it tells us about something that has already happened. Its main meaning is put in prison, or kept in prison. «The king imprisoned the knight for speaking out against him.» The clues are king, knight and speaking out: the knight was locked up as a punishment.
explain: The word can mean more than prison. «The lost puppy was imprisoned in a small cage.» There is no prison in that sentence, but the puppy could not get out, so imprisoned means kept somewhere and not able to get out. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The puppy was kept in a cage and could not get out" still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes imprisoned describes a feeling: «She felt imprisoned by fear.» Fear is not a building, so the word means unable to escape a feeling or situation. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Imprison means to put someone in prison, or to keep them somewhere they cannot leave.
fact: «Imprisoned» means put in prison as a punishment, or kept in prison.
fact: «Imprisoned» can also mean kept somewhere and not able to get out, like a trapped animal or a princess in a tower.
fact: In a figurative sense, «imprisoned» means unable to escape a feeling or situation, as in «imprisoned by fear».
fact: Useful phrases: «be imprisoned for», «wrongly imprisoned», «imprisoned in a tower».
exercise: «The thief was imprisoned for three years.» What does imprisoned mean here? | *Put in prison as a punishment | Set free to play | Painted a bright colour | Given a big prize
exercise: «The bird was imprisoned in a small cage.» What does imprisoned suggest? | Sleeping under a tree | Singing very loudly | *Kept somewhere and not able to get out | Flying high in the sky
exercise: «The knight was imprisoned in the tower and could not leave.» Which word tells you the knight was trapped? | *imprisoned | leave | tower | knight
test: «She felt imprisoned by fear, so she could not speak.» What does imprisoned mean here? | Lost in a forest | Very happy and free | Locked in a box | *Unable to escape the feeling of fear
test: Which phrase from this lesson means put in prison unfairly? | imprisoned by fear | *wrongly imprisoned | be imprisoned for | imprisoned in a tower
exam: Which sentence uses imprisoned in the figurative sense? | *«She felt imprisoned by her own worries.» | «He was imprisoned for stealing bread.» | «The bird was imprisoned in its cage.» | «The king imprisoned the spy in the tower.»
